---
import { featuredPokemonIds } from '../config/seo-pages';
import { pokemonById } from '../data/pokemon';
---
<section class="seo-content" aria-labelledby="how-title"><h2 id="how-title">Build a team you understand</h2><p>Choose up to six Pokémon, then review their type weaknesses, same-type offensive coverage and base-stat complementarity. Recommendations compare every eligible local candidate against your current team with the same scoring formula. You can add a teammate or choose a slot to replace, review the updated score.</p><h3>Start with a favorite</h3><div class="related-links">{featuredPokemonIds.map(id => <a href={`/pokemon/${id}/best-teammates`}>{pokemonById.get(id)!.name} teammates</a>)}</div><h3>Frequently asked questions</h3><details><summary>Does the score predict battle results?</summary><p>No. It is an explainable planning heuristic based on typing and base stats. It does not model moves, abilities, items, EVs, IVs, battle turns or opponent teams.</p></details><details><summary>Which Pokémon and rules are supported?</summary><p>The casual Generation 9 National Dex pool includes 1,025 base species. Alternate forms are not yet included. This is not a validator for VGC, Scarlet/Violet availability, ranked play or a Showdown competitive format.</p></details><details><summary>Can I save my team?</summary><p>Use Saved teams to keep a team in this browser. No account is required. Clearing browser data removes saved teams.</p></details><details><summary>Why can adding a Pokémon lower my score?</summary><p>Another teammate can introduce repeated weaknesses or reduce average attacking stats. The score does not award points just for filling slots. Incomplete teams are labeled provisional.</p></details></section>
